From a34553455de943e60626a0030d4dd3dded4d5a4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:57:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/82] OdfFile: drop a content control's trailing newline, not
 its tail

The code means to strip a trailing newline from a form control's text.
std::wstring::erase(size_type pos) takes a position and erases from it to
the end, so passing value.back() passes the character itself.

For the newline the guard has just tested, that is erase(10). A control
whose text is longer than ten characters is silently truncated to exactly
ten, at exit 0, with no warning. A shorter one throws std::out_of_range,
which surfaces as exit 80.

pop_back is what was meant.

The guard only fires on a real newline inside <w:t>, which is why this is
rarely seen: dump_text emits a literal backslash-n for paragraph breaks,
so value.back() is usually the letter n rather than a newline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
index 24653fc40d..95958787ec 100644
--- a/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
+++ b/OdfFile/Writer/Converter/DocxConverter.cpp
@@ -664,7 +664,7 @@ void DocxConverter::convert(OOX::Logic::CSdt *oox_sdt)
 		}
 		if ((false == value.empty()) && (value.back() == L'\n'))
 		{
-			value.erase(value.back());
+			value.pop_back();
 		}
 		// form:value and form:current-value are typed xsd:date on a date
 		// control, so the display string, "17/03/2024" and the like, is not a
